title: Walking on isometric maps
intro: An isometric map's solid diamonds are now walls: players walk over the diamonds, slide along the walls, and step from diamond to diamond.
project: Empty | Iso Walk

create: Tilemap
rename: Floor
set: Transform.Position = 0, 0, 0
set: Tilemap.Shape = Isometric
set: Tilemap.Tile Size = 2
set: Tilemap.Tint = #6FA860
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 11111111\n11111111\n11111111\n11111111\n11111111\n11111111\n11111111\n11111111
set: Tilemap.Solid = false
click: tiles:layer:+
rename: Walls
set: Tilemap.Tint = #9A8F86
set: Tilemap.Tiles = 22222222\n2......2\n2......2\n2..2...2\n2......2\n2......2\n2......2\n22222222
select: Main Camera
set: Transform.Position = 0, -4.5, 0
set: Camera.Size = 6

chapter: Walls shaped like diamonds | Solid, on an isometric map
select: Walls
look: 0, -4, 5
set: Tilemap.Solid = true
explain: world:-8, 0, 8, -8 | Solid diamonds | Here's an isometric room: a floor that doesn't collide, and a layer of walls with Solid on. Their solid tiles are now walls the shape of their diamonds, and the Scene view outlines them.

chapter: Walking over the ground | Top-down Movement, Isometric
deselect
create: Top-down Player
set: Transform.Position = 0, -6, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.6, 0.3
set: BoxCollider.Size = 0.6, 0.3
explain: component:TopDownMovement | A reminder | A top-down player on an isometric map gets a reminder in the Inspector.
set: TopDownMovement.Isometric = true
explain: field:TopDownMovement.Isometric | Isometric | Tick Isometric, and up and down go half as fast on the screen as left and right, the way the ground is seen at a slant. Its footprint is the diamond inside its collider, drawn in the Scene view.
play
hold: Up 0.5
hold: Right 2.5
expectat: Player = 5.7, -4
explain: game | Sliding along the wall | Walking straight right, it meets the wall's edge and slides along it, up into the corner, the way the wall runs on the screen.
hold: Down 3
expectat: Player = 0, -6.85
stop

chapter: A diamond at a time | Grid Movement
select: Player
key: Delete
deselect
create: Grid Player
set: Transform.Position = -3, -4, 0
play
wait: 0.3
expectat: Player = -3, -4
say: A grid player steps from diamond to diamond. Up steps up to the right, and left steps up to the left.
tap: Up
wait: 0.3
tap: Up
wait: 0.3
expectat: Player = -1, -3
tap: Right
wait: 0.3
expectat: Player = -1, -3
explain: game | Blocked | The pillar's diamond is down to the right, so pressing right bumps into it.
tap: Left
wait: 0.3
expectat: Player = -2, -2.5
say: Chasers, patrols, crates and pathfinding step over the diamonds the same way, and the Isometric template puts it all together.
stop
